+### Decisions & rationale (for the PR)
+- **`?slot=` on start (not a new route):** pre-declared by RC2.3 ("can be added in RC4.3 if the
+  UI demands it"); the §7.4 wireframe is per-row; absent = whole-application (back-compat).
+- **`corrected_name` column (expand-only):** the §8.3 edit-trio has a Name field; A1's
+  corrected-* pattern (snapshot immutable) extends naturally; the sweep + payload read the
+  effective name. The migration ships TWO additive columns (`corrected_name` + `corrected_at`), nothing destructive.
+- **Takeover only writes `taken_over_at`/`next_attempt_at` (never status):** `unreachable` is
+  terminal-sticky for every writer (AD-14), but §7.7 explicitly offers takeover from
+  unreachable — the takeover marker is not a status change, so stickiness is untouched and
+  the row can still late-complete (§8.6).
+- **Exhaustion at the failure sites (webhook + wrong-person), not the sweep:** AD-7's second
+  failure is a delivery/identity failure — it arrives via those routes; the sweep never sends
+  to awaiting_correction rows (NULL next_attempt_at) so it cannot observe the failure.
+- **Correction clears `terminal_reason` + the previous referee's session state
+  (`form_opened_at`/`draft_answers`, r2 W2); substitution keeps the old row untouched:** the
+  attempts log carries the history; the old row remains terminal evidence.
+- **Effective contact (r1 W4 / r2 W4):** once a correction ran (`correction_cycles >= 1`)
+  the snapshot is PROVEN DEAD — the corrected values ARE the contact and a cleared channel
+  stays absent (AD-7 never-re-contact). The rule applies in the sweep, the webhook's
+  send-ref fallback, the expired-link resend (form_handler), and the client prefill.
+- **Substitution guard rails (r2 W5/W7):** an unchanged save of the terminal referee's own
+  trio is a 400 (Art 21 route-around); re-substituting the HISTORY row with different
+  details is a 409 — the typed referee is never silently dropped.
+- **App trio updated by both correct and substitute:** A1's "edits the slot's trio inline"
