+-- RC4.3 r1 (Perkins W6): "Start this check now" on an application whose rows
+-- already exist (the viewed trigger created them) is an idempotent no-op in
+-- the insert — the honest re-arm: nudge every queued row for the application
+-- to due-now so the cadence sweep picks them up on the next tick. Guarded on
+-- queued + not-taken-over (A7: a landlord-handled row is never re-armed).
+-- 0 rows is fine (nothing queued) — the caller treats the re-arm as best-effort.
+--- rearm_queued_reference_calls(application_id: UUID, ref_slot: TEXT)
+UPDATE reference_call
+SET next_attempt_at = now(),
+    updated_at = now()
+WHERE application_id = $1
+  -- r2 (N4): per-slot re-arm when the landlord started ONE slot — the other
+  -- slot stays untouched; '' re-arms the whole application.
+  AND ($2 = '' OR ref_slot = $2)
+  AND status = 'queued'::reference_call_status
+  AND taken_over_at IS NULL
+RETURNING id::text;
